What is a Document Library?
   A Document Library is a container inside a SharePoint Site specifically designed to store and manage files.

A library can contain files such as:
      Word
      Excel
      PowerPoint
      PDF
      Images
      Text files
      Other supported business files

When you create a Document Library, it normally inherits permissions from the SharePoint Site.

   Example:
   
   Budget Approval Site
   
         Owners → Full Control
         Members → Edit
         Visitors → Read

↓

Budget Documents Library inherits those same permissions.
So you don't need to configure security again.

But you can give the library different permissions
Suppose you create:
Confidential Budget Documents Library and only Finance Managers should access it.
   
   You can:
   
      Go to Library permissions
      Stop/Break permission inheritance
      Remove the inherited groups/users as appropriate
      Add Finance Managers
      Give them the required permission, such as Edit/Read
